# Issue commit linking (GitHub)

Applies to **GitHub issue mode** commits. **Roadmap mode** uses `[P<n>]` + `Task: P<n>` instead — see `02-git-workflow.mdc`.

Every **issue-related** commit must reference **GitHub `#N` only** — never Kaneo task IDs.

Bidirectional Kaneo ↔ GitHub sync is active for `mdg-labs/berth`. Kaneo task IDs are for MCP status updates only; they must not appear in git.

## Required subject format

```
<type>(<scope>)[#N]: <imperative summary>
```

| Part | Rule |
|------|------|
| `<type>` | Conventional Commits: `feat`, `fix`, `chore`, `refactor`, `docs`, `test`, `ci`, `build`, `perf` |
| `<scope>` | Allowed scopes from `02-git-workflow.mdc` |
| `[#N]` | **Mandatory** — GitHub issue number on `mdg-labs/berth` |
| Summary | Imperative mood; whole subject ≤72 chars |

## Required body format

```
fixes #N
```

Place on its own line. Repo default `mdg-labs/berth` — no need for full `owner/repo#N` in body when working in this repo.

## Forbidden

- Kaneo task IDs in subject or body (`d4fd7ibt0agftmlv0bi8lcze`)
- `Task: …` Kaneo footers in commits
- Referencing Kaneo task `number` instead of GitHub issue number when they differ (they should match for synced tasks)

## Epic (parent) issues

When orchestrator passes `PARENT: #P`:

| Commit | Subject | Body |
|--------|---------|------|
| Subtask | `[#<leaf>][#<P>]` | `fixes #<leaf>` + `refs #<P>` |
| Final child closing epic | `[#<leaf>][#<P>]` | + `fixes #<P>` when P in `CLOSE_PARENTS` |

## Verifier / orchestrator audit

```bash
git log <base>..HEAD --grep='fixes #N'
```

Missing → **FAIL** — do not mark Done.

## Exceptions (no issue key)

- Roadmap commits: `[P6]` format
- Pure repo hygiene outside orchestrator (rare)
